  "explanation": "We replace the reference square pulse with a smoothly-shaped \u03a9(t) and a time-dependent detuning \u03b4(t) optimized via L-BFGS-B with direct Hamiltonian integration (10 substeps/ns). The key insight: at weak blockade (r\u2082 = 6.5\u00b5m, V/\u03a9 = 1.8), the square pulse leaks 22% population into |rr\u27e9 because the interaction is too weak to suppress double excitation. Our shaped pulse starts \u03b4(t) far blue-detuned (\u221246 rad/\u00b5s), which increases the |s\u27e9\u2013|rr\u27e9 gap to V \u2212 \u03b4 \u2248 57 rad/\u00b5s, then sweeps \u03b4(t) through resonance mid-pulse to actively de-excite any residual |rr\u27e9 population through the \u03a9-coupled |s\u27e9 channel. The smooth \u03a9 envelope (0 \u2192 8 \u2192 0 rad/\u00b5s) and long duration (T = 1500 ns) ensure adiabaticity. At strong blockade (r\u2081 = 5.0\u00b5m, V/\u03a9 = 8.8) the same strategy further suppresses the residual |rr\u27e9 from 0.6% to < 10\u207b\u00b9\u00b2."
